-- 042: Deep content + matching exercises for X06 · Data Visualization.
UPDATE public.sessions SET
 content_en = E'## Why a chart is an argument, not decoration\n\nA chart''s job is to make one point land in seconds. The wrong chart — or an honest chart drawn carelessly — buries the point or, worse, misleads. This lesson is about choosing and shaping charts that argue clearly and fairly.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Choose the chart for the question\n\nStart from the *type of question*, not the data:\n\n| Question type | Best chart | Example |\n|---------------|-----------|---------|\n| **Comparison** (which is bigger?) | Bar column | Revenue by region |\n| **Trend** (how does it change over time?) | Line | Monthly revenue |\n| **Composition** (parts of a whole) | Stacked bar / 100% bar | Category share per month |\n| **Distribution** (how are values spread?) | Histogram / box plot | Basket-size spread |\n| **Relationship** (do two move together?) | Scatter | Discount vs returns |\n\n> Pie charts work only for 2–3 slices. Beyond that, a bar chart compares far more accurately.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Color and layout that help, not hurt\n\n- **Limit colour.** Use one accent to highlight the point; grey everything else. A rainbow chart has no focus.\n- **Order intentionally.** Sort bars by value, not alphabetically, unless the category order carries meaning.\n- **Label directly.** Put values or labels on the marks instead of making readers hop to a legend.\n- **Consistent scales.** Same colour = same meaning across every chart in a report.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Story with data (Knaflic)\n\nOne chart, **one message**. Write the takeaway as the chart *title*: not "Revenue by Month" but "Revenue grew 22% after the April relaunch". The chart then exists to support that sentence, and you strip everything that does not.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Anti-patterns that mislead\n\n| Anti-pattern | Why it misleads |\n|--------------|-----------------|\n| **Truncated y-axis** | A tiny difference looks huge — start bar axes at 0 |\n| **3D charts** | Perspective distorts the real sizes |\n| **Dual axes** | Implies a correlation that may not exist |\n| **Too many pie slices** | The eye cannot compare angles |\n| **Rainbow palette** | No visual hierarchy, nothing stands out |\n\n> **Mini case study.** A team showed "flat" sales on a 0–100M axis. Re-drawn on a 0–5M axis (the real range) with the growth month highlighted in one colour, the same data clearly showed a 22% jump — and got the budget approved.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| Comparison chart | Shows which category is larger (bar) |\n| Trend chart | Shows change over time (line) |\n| Composition chart | Shows parts of a whole (stacked/100% bar) |\n| Truncated axis | An axis not starting at zero, exaggerating differences |\n| Direct labelling | Values placed on the marks, not in a legend |\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. Pick the chart from the **question type**: comparison→bar, trend→line, composition→stacked, distribution→histogram, relationship→scatter.\n2. **One chart, one message** — put the takeaway in the title.\n3. Use colour sparingly to highlight; grey the rest.\n4. Avoid truncated axes, 3D, dual axes, and overloaded pies — they mislead.\n5. Label directly and order bars by value.\n\n> 💡 Practice with the matching exercises below, then build one clear chart for the assignment case.',
 content_id = E'## Kenapa chart adalah argumen, bukan hiasan\n\nTugas sebuah chart adalah membuat satu poin tersampaikan dalam hitungan detik. Chart yang salah — atau chart jujur yang digambar sembarangan — mengubur poin atau, lebih buruk, menyesatkan. Pelajaran ini soal memilih dan membentuk chart yang berargumen jelas dan adil.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pilih chart sesuai pertanyaan\n\nMulai dari *jenis pertanyaan*, bukan datanya:\n\n| Jenis pertanyaan | Chart terbaik | Contoh |\n|------------------|---------------|--------|\n| **Perbandingan** (mana lebih besar?) | Bar/kolom | Revenue per region |\n| **Tren** (bagaimana berubah seiring waktu?) | Line | Revenue bulanan |\n| **Komposisi** (bagian dari keseluruhan) | Stacked bar / 100% bar | Porsi kategori per bulan |\n| **Distribusi** (bagaimana nilai menyebar?) | Histogram / box plot | Sebaran basket size |\n| **Hubungan** (apakah dua bergerak bersama?) | Scatter | Diskon vs retur |\n\n> Pie chart hanya cocok untuk 2–3 irisan. Lebih dari itu, bar chart membandingkan jauh lebih akurat.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Warna dan layout yang membantu, bukan menyakiti\n\n- **Batasi warna.** Pakai satu aksen untuk menyoroti poin; abu-abukan sisanya. Chart pelangi tak punya fokus.\n- **Urutkan sengaja.** Urutkan bar berdasarkan nilai, bukan abjad, kecuali urutan kategori bermakna.\n- **Label langsung.** Taruh nilai/label di mark alih-alih memaksa pembaca melompat ke legenda.\n- **Skala konsisten.** Warna sama = makna sama di setiap chart dalam laporan.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Story with data (Knaflic)\n\nSatu chart, **satu pesan**. Tulis kesimpulan sebagai *judul* chart: bukan "Revenue per Bulan" tapi "Revenue tumbuh 22% setelah relaunch April". Chart lalu ada untuk mendukung kalimat itu, dan Anda buang semua yang tidak.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Anti-pattern yang menyesatkan\n\n| Anti-pattern | Kenapa menyesatkan |\n|--------------|--------------------|\n| **Sumbu-y terpotong** | Beda kecil terlihat besar — mulai sumbu bar dari 0 |\n| **Chart 3D** | Perspektif mendistorsi ukuran sebenarnya |\n| **Dua sumbu** | Menyiratkan korelasi yang mungkin tak ada |\n| **Terlalu banyak irisan pie** | Mata tak bisa membandingkan sudut |\n| **Palet pelangi** | Tak ada hierarki visual, tak ada yang menonjol |\n\n> **Studi kasus mini.** Sebuah tim menampilkan penjualan "datar" pada sumbu 0–100M. Digambar ulang pada sumbu 0–5M (rentang nyata) dengan bulan pertumbuhan disorot satu warna, data yang sama jelas menunjukkan lonjakan 22% — dan anggaran pun disetujui.\n\n---\n\n## Glosarium\n\n| Istilah | Arti |\n|---------|------|\n| Chart perbandingan | Menunjukkan kategori mana lebih besar (bar) |\n| Chart tren | Menunjukkan perubahan seiring waktu (line) |\n| Chart komposisi | Menunjukkan bagian dari keseluruhan (stacked/100% bar) |\n| Sumbu terpotong | Sumbu yang tak mulai dari nol, melebih-lebihkan beda |\n| Pelabelan langsung | Nilai ditaruh di mark, bukan di legenda |\n\n---\n\n## Kesimpulan Utama\n\n1. Pilih chart dari **jenis pertanyaan**: perbandingan→bar, tren→line, komposisi→stacked, distribusi→histogram, hubungan→scatter.\n2. **Satu chart, satu pesan** — taruh kesimpulan di judul.\n3. Pakai warna hemat untuk menyoroti; abu-abukan sisanya.\n4. Hindari sumbu terpotong, 3D, dua sumbu, dan pie berlebih — menyesatkan.\n5. Label langsung dan urutkan bar berdasarkan nilai.\n\n> 💡 Latih dengan exercise matching di bawah, lalu buat satu chart yang jelas untuk case tugas.'
WHERE session_number = 'X06';

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'Question to Chart Type', 'Pertanyaan ke Jenis Chart',
  'Match each question type to the best chart.', 'Cocokkan setiap jenis pertanyaan dengan chart terbaik.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Which region is biggest?","right":"Bar chart"},{"left":"How did revenue change over months?","right":"Line chart"},{"left":"Category share of the total","right":"Stacked bar"},{"left":"Do discount and returns move together?","right":"Scatter plot"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Bar chart","description_en":"Comparison","description_id":"Perbandingan","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Line chart","description_en":"Trend","description_id":"Tren","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Stacked bar","description_en":"Composition","description_id":"Komposisi","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Scatter plot","description_en":"Relationship","description_id":"Hubungan","points":25}]',
  '["Time series wants a line","Two numerics want a scatter"]','["Deret waktu pakai line","Dua angka pakai scatter"]','easy',1
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X06' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='Question to Chart Type');

